Wagon door controller
=====================

Setup
-----
- Orient this programmable block with its Forward axis toward the wagon's
  chosen front and its Right axis toward the wagon's right side.
- Add [DOOR_LEFT] to the Custom Name of every door on the wagon's local left
  side, and [DOOR_RIGHT] to every door on its local right side. These sides are
  defined while looking toward the programmable block's Forward direction.
- Tagged doors must be on the same grid as this programmable block. A door with
  both tags is ignored.

The wagon listens for locomotive commands over IGC on the connected-constructs
range; no train ID configuration is needed. It compares its own
programmable-block orientation with the locomotive's direction and swaps the
door sides when the wagon is facing backward. If the orientation is ambiguous,
it closes tagged doors instead of guessing.

Tagged door blocks are enabled while moving to their commanded state, then
disabled once fully open or closed. Players cannot operate disabled doors.

This direction comparison works when each wagon's heading is within 60 degrees
of the locomotive's heading (or its opposite when reversed). A wagon more than
90 degrees around a tight curve can be mistaken for a reversed wagon; a long
consist spread around a loop may need a neighbor-to-neighbor orientation
protocol instead.
